    externalId: "policy-code-of-conduct-policy",
    title: "Code of Conduct Policy",
    sourceType: "policy",
    content: "Code of Conduct Policy\nSolsphere AI Inc.| Regodit\nIntroduction\nAt Solsphere, our Code of Conduct is designed to provide clear and actionable guidelines for all employees, contractors, and affiliates. These standards ensure that everyone within the company acts ethically and with integrity, both professionally and personally. This document serves as a comprehensive tool to guide employees through ethical decision-making, foster a culture of respect, transparency, fairness, and accountability, and protect the company’s integrity. These policies are essential to promoting a positive workplace and ensuring compliance with laws and company guidelines.\nThe Code of Conduct applies to all personnel at all levels of the organization. Whether directly employed or contracted, all individuals working on behalf of Solsphere must adhere to these principles in every aspect of their business interactions.\n1. Ethical Standards for Employee Behavior\nHonesty, Integrity, and Respect\nEmployees must uphold honesty in every communication, action, and decision, ensuring that they are truthful and transparent with colleagues, clients, partners, and customers. Integrity is central to our culture; it means doing the right thing even in the absence of supervision. Employees should act ethically, keep their commitments, and take responsibility for their actions. Respect involves treating others with dignity, valuing diversity, and refraining from behaviors that could be perceived as offensive, derogatory, or discriminatory. All employees should engage in decision-making processes that reflect the highest ethical standards.\nIf an employee is uncertain about the ethical implications of an action or decision, they should consult with management or the ethics committee for guidance.\nProfessional Conduct\nEmployees are expected to maintain professionalism in all areas, including verbal and non-verbal communication. This includes respecting differences of opinion and maintaining a courteous tone during conversations, even in stressful situations. Unprofessional behavior, such as offensive language, public disagreements, or inappropriate conduct, will not be tolerated.\n2. Non-Discrimination, Harassment, and Bullying\nPolicy on Discrimination, Harassment, and Bullying\nSolsphere is committed to providing a workplace that is free from all forms of discrimination, harassment, and bullying. Employees must treat one another with dignity, respect, and fairness, regardless of age, gender, race, ethnicity, sexual orientation, religion, disability, or nationality. Discrimination in any form, whether subtle or overt, is strictly prohibited. Harassment includes unwelcome conduct that creates a hostile, intimidating, or offensive work environment and can take physical, verbal, or visual forms. Employees must not engage in bullying behaviors that undermine or harm colleagues’ emotional, physical, or social well-being.\nEqual Opportunity and Fair Treatment\n At Solsphere, we are committed to ensuring all employment decisions—hiring, promotions, training, and compensation—are based solely on qualifications and performance. All employees are entitled to equal treatment and opportunity, free from bias, prejudice, or favoritism. Our hiring and promotion processes are designed to recognize individual merit and capabilities.\n3. Conflicts of Interest\nDisclosure and Management of Conflicts of Interest\nA conflict of interest occurs when an employee’s personal interests interfere with their ability to act in the best interest of Solsphere. Conflicts may be financial, personal, or relational in nature. It is crucial that employees disclose potential conflicts, whether real or perceived, to the Senior Management and / or Head of Human Resources. This transparency ensures that conflicts are addressed in a timely and effective manner. For example, if an employee holds a financial interest in a supplier or vendor, they must disclose this information and recuse themselves from related decision-making processes.\nAvoiding Conflicts of Interest\nEmployees should always prioritize the interests of Solsphere over personal gain. Avoiding situations where personal relationships or financial interests could compromise or even appear to compromise professional decision-making is critical. Employees must also refrain from engaging in personal business transactions that could create a conflict or the perception of bias in their professional role.\n4. Gifts, Hospitality, and Benefits\nGuidelines on Accepting and Giving Gifts\nEmployees must avoid accepting or offering gifts, hospitality, or other benefits that could influence, or be perceived to influence, business decisions. Modest gifts or hospitality (e.g., a meal or small token of appreciation) may be acceptable, but lavish or frequent exchanges are discouraged. Gifts intended to establish a personal relationship or influence decisions could raise ethical concerns. Employees should use their discretion when evaluating such situations.\nDisclosure Requirements\nEmployees must report any gifts or benefits they receive or offer that exceed a specific threshold. Reports should be made to the compliance department or human resources. Any gift exceeding the specified value will be reviewed for potential conflicts of interest or ethical concerns. Transparency ensures that the company can maintain its commitment to fairness and impartiality.\nBusiness Meals and Entertainment\nBusiness meals and entertainment are acceptable only when they are reasonable, appropriate for the context, and not intended to influence decision-making. When engaging in these activities, employees should always act in accordance with the company’s values and adhere to reasonable limits.\n5. Insider Trading and Confidential Information\nProhibition of Insider Trading\nInsider trading is the illegal practice of using non-public, material information to make financial gains in securities trading. Employees are prohibited from using or disclosing confidential com",
    author: "Solsphere AI Inc. (Regodit)",
    scope: "all personnel",
    sourceDate: "2026-08-01",
    effectiveFrom: "2026-08-01",
    reliability: "high",
